==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Raclesa, type Σ''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
A Floating Tank and DPS hybrid with very good stats across the board, this uber-strong gal has viable matchups against practically all enemies within her trait. Raclesa already hits for very high damage even against untargeted enemies; that said, her numbers are bumped up to 107,406 DPH through [[Strong Against]] when up against Floating adversaries, which translates to ~14,200 DPS at just Lv.30. The [[Omni Strike]] is just the icing on the cake; pesky peons won't be capable of intercepting her as easily because of it.

Her attacks also have a guaranteed chance to [[Slow]] Floating, which is primarily useful for the enemies she doesn't immediately kill (Floating [[Teacher Bun Bun|Bun Buns]] and [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s). The main issue in application is that she is outranged by a majority of her more notable targets like [[Cli-One]], rendering its activation irrelevant if they don't take a damage knockback. Regardless, it is still a very good control effect against aggressive frontliners, such as the Bun Bun variants.

While her foreswing is lengthy, it is not only mitigated with her Omni Attack, but also works to her benefit to juggle floating pushers. She will start her attack right when her slow effect ends, allowing enemies to rush to her range just to be slammed by her mace and get slowed again, and this cycle can repeat to crush floating pushers.

Raclesa has an absurdly high effective HP of 420,750 (668,235 at Lv.50) against Floating enemies, which gives her more than enough bulk to tank even [[J.K. Bun Bun]]s head-on without even flinching. Thanks to her various immunities, she can even be used reliably against [[Gobble]]s and [[Zollow]]s, something that a majority of anti-Floating units fail to achieve. What's more, she also can't be Cursed, allowing her to pummel her way right through [[Othom]] and [[Lowkey]], while giving her use in mixed [[Uncanny Legends]] stages.

Even outside of Floating enemies, Raclesa can prove to be a solid generalist thanks to her above-average DPS for her range, quick cooldown, wide array of debuff immunities and colossal bulk, which help separate her from your standard [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]], and help her viability on mixed stages.

All in all, while simple, Raclesa is a powerful [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating unit]] and provides good coverage for the entirety of her target trait, while also being a decent generalist.

